SUMMARY:"Life's a Beach!" Fundraiser
DESCRIPTION:The Rotary Club of Santa Rosa East/West invites you to our annual fundraiser! Get ready to put the FUN in fundraiser at our “Life’s a Beach” themed event. Don your best beach attire or Hawaiian shirt and prepare for an unforgettable evening of dancing\, trivia\, beach ball games\, limbo contests\, photo opportunities\, and so much more. \nEnjoy a delicious buffet dinner by Sally Tomatoes\, drinks from our hosted bar\, and indulge in our dessert frenzy! This festive celebration will feature a paddle raise benefiting the 6th Street Studio\, plus exciting silent and live auctions with amazing prizes. From our popular wine fridge to incredible auction items\, there will be plenty of opportunities to bid\, win\, and support a great cause. \nTickets are $150 per person. To register and buy tickets\, click the link below. After you register\, you will be contacted for payment. Credit cards and checks are accepted.. Checks can also be mailed to the Rotary Club of Santa Rosa East/West to PO Box 2785\, Santa Rosa\, CA 95405. Make checks payable to the Rotary Club of Santa Rosa East/West Foundation. \nClick here for tickets: https://www.sreastwestrotary.org/events-1/lifesabeach \nSponsorship opportunities are available and can be purchased using the link above. \nEvery year the Rotary Club of Santa Rosa East/West holds an event to raise money to support Rotary International’s goals\, as well as many local charitable organizations. We not only contribute time\, talent and dollars to a number of on-going programs\, we also select a worthy cause to become a primary beneficiary of additional funds raised at this event. We are pleased to announce that the primary beneficiary for this year’s fundraiser is the 6th Street Studio. They offer live performance programs for all youth\, regardless of situation\, to creatively express\, explore and grow through theater arts. The funds raised at this event will go toward their youth programs. \nThe 6th Street Studio’s mission is to engage their community in an empowering and accessible educational space in which all people\, regardless of age\, socioeconomic status\, race\, religion\, or ability\, can creatively express\, explore\, and grow through theater arts. 6th Street Studio education programs foster community\, creativity\, and empathy through play! \nQuestions?: If you have any questions about this event\, please contact Mae Heagerty-Matos at mae_matos@yahoo.com or 650-773-6418. If you have questions about buying tickets or the registration process\, please contact Julie Montgomery at julielovesrotary@gmail.com or 707-328-5905. If you have questions about sponsoring the event\, please contact Brian Reed at breed@summitstatebank.com. \nThank you for supporting the Rotary Club of Santa Rosa East/West and we look forward to seeing you at the event!
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/lifes-a-beach/
LOCATION:Finley Community Center\, 2060 West College Avenue\, Santa Rosa\, CA
CATEGORIES:Other
GEO:38.4441;-122.749
