SUMMARY:Sonoma County Philharmonic presents Fanny\, Florence & Sam
DESCRIPTION:Norman Gamboa\, conductor\nEsther Rayo\, soprano \nCOLERIDGE-TAYLOR Idyll\, Op.44\nMENDELSSOHN Hero und Leander\nPRICE Symphony No. 1 \nJoin us for a program featuring three under- appreciated composers whose works are finally receiving the attention they deserve. \n♪ Samuel Coleridge-Taylor’s lovely Idyll sets a reflective and poetic tone with its tender melodies and pastoral elegance. \n♪ Fanny Mendelssohn’s dramatic cantata\, Hero und Leander\, weaves a tragic Greek myth into music of passion and vivid orchestration. \n♪ Florence Price’s groundbreaking Symphony No. 1 blends classical forms with African American spirituals and folk rhythms creating an iconic 20th century American masterpiece. \nCome celebrate the breadth of orchestral music and its enduring power to surprise\, delight\, and move the human spirit!
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/sonoma-county-philharmonic-presents-fanny-florence-sam-2/
LOCATION:Jackson Theater at Sonoma Country Day School\, 4400 Day School Place\, Santa Rosa\, CA
CATEGORIES:Music
